        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C12219"/>
        <NHC0>R145</NHC0>
        <P106>Conceptual Entity</P106>
        <P107>Has Physical Location</P107>
        <P108>Gene_Has_Physical_Location</P108>
        <P90>Gene_Has_Physical_Location</P90>
        <P97>A role used to link a gene with its physical extent on a chromosome, denoted by the chromosome number and start and end base positions (with numbering beginning at the telomere of the short p arm). The domain and range for this role are &apos;Gene&apos; and &apos;Anatomic Structure, System, or Substance&apos;, respectively.</P97>
        <P98>The standard for the numbering system is that assigned by the Human Genome Consortium and found at Entrez Gene. The role is considered as supplementary to the role Gene_In Chromosomal_Location</P98>
        <rdfs:label>Gene_Has_Physical_Location</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#R145"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#P90"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Gene_Has_Physical_Location</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <P383>PT</P383>
        <P384>NCI</P384>
    </owl:Axiom>
