        <P90>Procedure_Has_Target_Anatomy</P90>
        <P97>A role used to assert a relationship between a procedure and its target anatomy, specifically that a particular procedure always has an association with the target anatomy. This role should be used when a more specific role cannot be asserted, including procedures targeting blood and other fluids. The domain and range for this role are &apos;Clinical or Research Activity&apos; and &apos;Anatomic Structure, System, or Substance&apos;, respectively.</P97>
        <rdfs:label>Procedure_Has_Target_Anatomy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
