        <P108>Disease_Mapped_To_Chromosome</P108>
        <P90>Disease_Mapped_To_Chromosome</P90>
        <P95>If Disease_Has_Cytogenetic_Abnormality is present, then don&apos;t assert the Disease_Mapped_To_Chromosome role.</P95>
        <P97>A role used to assert a relationship between a disease, disorder or finding and a chromosome. This restriction should be used when a disease or disorder maps to a chromosome.  It is not meant to be used when a specific cytogenetic abnormality is known (e.g. translocation, inversion). The domain and range for this role are &apos;Disease, Disorder or Finding&apos; and &apos;Chromosome&apos;, respectively. The range for this role excludes chromosomal bands and physical locations.</P97>
        <rdfs:label>Disease_Mapped_To_Chromosome</rdfs:label>
