        <P107>Found In Organism</P107>
        <P108>Gene_Found_In_Organism</P108>
        <P90>Gene_Found_In_Organism</P90>
        <P97>A role used to specify the organism of origin for a gene. It may be used to differentiate genes with the same name and functions that originate from different organisms. The domain and range for this role are &apos;Gene&apos; and &apos;Organism&apos;, respectively.</P97>
        <P98>Currently, we only model human genes, but this role has obvious utility in future, if other organisms are modeled as well.</P98>
        <rdfs:label>Gene_Found_In_Organism</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
