    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C13199">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C22188"/>
        <NHC0>C13199</NHC0>
        <P106>Cell Component</P106>
        <P108>Chloroplast</P108>
        <P207>C0008266</P207>
        <P366>Chloroplast</P366>
        <P90>Chloroplast</P90>
        <P97>Photosynthetic organelle containing chlorophyll, the photosynthetic pigment, in cells of leaves and young stems of higher plants. Lens-shaped and rather variable in size but approximately 5 m long. Surrounded by a double membrane and contains circular DNA (though not enough to code for all proteins in the chloroplast). Like the mitochondrion, it is semi-autonomous. It resembles a cyanobacterium from which, on the endosymbiont hypothesis, it might be derived. Chlorophyll is associated with the membrane of vesicles (thylakoids) that are stacked to form grana.</P97>
        <rdfs:label>Chloroplast</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C13199"/>
