        <P106>Gene or Genome</P106>
        <P107>Telomere Maintenance Gene</P107>
        <P108>Telomere Maintenance Gene</P108>
        <P207>C1336700</P207>
        <P322>CTRP</P322>
        <P366>Telomere_Maintenance_Gene</P366>
        <P90>Telomere Maintenance Gene</P90>
        <P97>Telomere Maintenance Genes encode specialized proteins bound to telomeric DNA repeats and directly involved in maintaining/protecting chromosome telomere ends to prevent a damage response that halts cell proliferation. Telomerase, which lengthens telomeric DNA by RNA-templated addition of repeated DNA sequences, is regulated by proteins that bind to the telomeric DNA repeats and to additional proteins to assemble a higher-order telomeric complex. (NCI)</P97>
        <rdfs:label>Telomere Maintenance Gene</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C20338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#P90"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Telomere Maintenance Gene</owl:annotatedTarget>
