        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#P97"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Telomere Maintenance Genes encode specialized proteins bound to telomeric DNA repeats and directly involved in maintaining/protecting chromosome telomere ends to prevent a damage response that halts cell proliferation. Telomerase, which lengthens telomeric DNA by RNA-templated addition of repeated DNA sequences, is regulated by proteins that bind to the telomeric DNA repeats and to additional proteins to assemble a higher-order telomeric complex. (NCI)</owl:annotatedTarget>
