        <P325>The originating point of the Content Item or record, including but not limited to archive import, Scan, fax, email, paper form.</P325>
        <P325>The specific permanent record(s) upon which a user will rely for the reconstruction and evaluation of a clinical investigation. NOTE:  The term identifies records planned (designated by the protocol) or referenced as the ones that provide the information underlying the analyses and findings of a clinical investigation. Accuracy, suitability, and trustworthiness are not defining attributes of &quot;source.&quot; The term is also sometimes used as shorthand for source documents and/or source data.  [After ICH E6, CSUICI] See also source document, source data, original data, certified copy.</P325>
        <P366>Source</P366>
        <P370>TCGA</P370>
        <P90>Source</P90>
        <P90>source</P90>
