        <P322>CDISC-GLOSS</P322>
        <P322>MRCT-Ctr</P322>
        <P325>Bias refers to defects in study design, measurement, analysis or interpretation such that they cause a result to depart from the true value in a consistent direction. [after AMA Manual of style, ICH E9, CONSORT Statement]</P325>
        <P325>Flaws in the way a study is designed, done, or analyzed that lead to one conclusion being favored over another. (https://mrctcenter.org/glossaryterm/research-bias/)</P325>
        <P325>In a clinical trial, a flaw in the study design or method of collecting or interpreting information.  Biases can lead to incorrect conclusions about what the study or trial showed.</P325>
