        <P207>C1327622</P207>
        <P366>Regulation</P366>
        <P90>Regulation</P90>
        <P90>Regulatory Process</P90>
        <P95>The current principles of organization of Biological Processes are adopted largely from the Gene Ontology (GO). According to GO, any regulatory process is a direct child of the process that it regulates, satisfying an &apos;IS A&apos; relationship with its parent. Consistent with this, all terms considered for entry to Regulation should be actually located under the appropriate class that they regulate.  March 25, 2010 John Bradsher</P95>
        <P97>A process that acts to control the rate or manner in which another process progresses or a product is formed.</P97>
        <rdfs:label>Regulatory Process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
